@model IEnumerable<Student>
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Reports"; var byCourse = Model.GroupBy(s => s.Course).OrderBy(g => g.Key); }
<div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center mb-4">
    <div>
        <h1 class="h2 mb-1">Reports</h1>
        <p class="text-muted mb-0">Student enrollment summary by course.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="d-flex gap-2">
        <button id="exportCsvBtn" type="button" class="btn btn-outline-success btn-sm">Export to CSV</button>
        <button id="printReportBtn" type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm">Print Report</button>
        <span class="badge text-bg-primary fs-6 align-self-center">@Model.Count() students</span>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="card border-0 shadow-sm">
    <div class="card-body p-4">
        <table id="reportsTable" class="table mb-0">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Course</th>
                    <th class="text-end">Enrolled students</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
@foreach (var group in byCourse) {
                <tr>
                    <td>@group.Key</td>
                    <td class="text-end">@group.Count()</td>
                </tr>
}
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>

@section Scripts {
    <script src="~/js/reports.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
}
